    "behavior": [
      "Spring owns ticker normalization, the public controller, explicit 25-field top-level response DTO, application query use case, and transport-neutral immutable structured projection",
      "all nested fields, insertion order, nulls, arrays, booleans, strings, and numeric values are preserved without exposing Jackson, HTTP, SEC, cache-client, or Node transport types to application or domain",
      "profile, quote, financials, score, buyScore, filings, irMaterials, highlights, peerGroup, bottleneck, narrative, capitalFlow, cashFlowQuality, multipleInsight, guidanceInsight, timeframeView, correctionAssessment, thesisMonitor, reversalConfirmation, sectorContext, verdicts, bottomSignal, positionSizing, executionBridge, and peers are required in the legacy projection",
      "successful detail projections are fresh for five minutes and usable as stale for at most thirty minutes while one background refresh per normalized ticker executes",
      "detail projection and serialized payload cache cardinality are each bounded to 128 tickers; malformed, unavailable, and 404 responses never replace a successful value",
      "serialized bytes are reused only while the same immutable application projection instance remains current, so inbound serialization caching cannot extend data freshness",
      "identity JSON field order and bytes match Node, while gzip only changes the negotiated wire representation"
